# Source art and unoptimised exports. tools/optimize.py turns raw/ into
# assets/img/; the outputs are committed, the inputs are not.
#
# This is not tidiness. A previous repo in this family shipped 22 MB of raw
# generation renders to a public GitHub repo, and they stayed downloadable from
# raw.githubusercontent.com long after the Pages site was cleaned. The art is
# reproducible from the recipes in docs/BRIEF.md; the blobs never need to be.
raw/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

_site/

# The IT platform's config for THIS landing: the landing_id IT gave it, and
# nothing else. Written on the server, never committed. A copied id from
# another landing sends registrations there (CAMPAIGN.md step 4).
config.json

# tools/handoff.py writes the IT archive here. It is a build output of
# committed files: reproducible in one command, and 400 kB of zip nobody
# should be diffing.
dist/

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# Scratch for agents: notes, screenshots, specs.
out/
